const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文围绕股票拆分信息研究价格如何在事件时间内调整，展示早期事件研究的组织方式。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper studies stock-price adjustment around stock-split information and illustrates an early event-study organization. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源把事件、收益和市场比较放入事件窗口，重点是信息时点与正常回报基准的定义。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It places an event, returns, and a market comparison in an event window, making information timing and normal-return baseline central. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要原始公告时间、拆分与股息资料、复权价格、市场指数、交易日历和事件样本筛选规则。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Use original announcement times, split and dividend data, adjusted prices, a market index, a trading calendar, and event-sample rules. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"该研究说明事件时间分析依赖准确的事件和基准构造，而不是说明每一条新闻都会产生同一种价格反应。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"It shows that event-time analysis depends on accurate event and benchmark construction, not that all news generates the same price response. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"区分公告、传闻、实施和交易所生效日期，处理事件重叠和停牌，并保存使用的复权及基准版本。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Separate announcement, rumor, implementation, and exchange-effective dates; handle overlapping events and halts; retain adjustment and benchmark versions. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 International Economic Review (1969)。历史股票拆分样本和市场制度不等于当前事件的因果模板；该导读不输出异常收益或交易信号。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites International Economic Review (1969). A historical split sample and market institution are not a causal template for a current event, and this guide produces no abnormal-return signal. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史股票拆分样本和市场制度不等于当前事件的因果模板；该导读不输出异常收益或交易信号。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
